From 29feb4d422bcea51bfa1c832e6a659e2ec5fccf9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bugcheck <bugcheck@local>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 02:37:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/10] Traffic: cars use the road freely (lane changes,
 overtaking, kerb stops)

Cars could never change lanes (only buses), so a car in the wrong lane for a turn
had to go round the block (right-right-right = the '270 deg' left turn; routes
+550 m median, up to +2.2 km at 157 of 430 multi-lane approaches).

- Lane changes: one lane at a time, gap acceptance on the target lane, the body
  slides over (existing lat offset) and stays an obstacle in the old lane until
  it has left it. Checked once per second per car (4x while a turn needs it).
- Turns owned by a neighbouring lane are planned ('folded'), reached by a lane
  change before the junction; routing (route_drivable/_lane_path) does the same
  with a cost that grows on short blocks. An ambient car that can't get over in
  time skips that turn (never turns across the neighbour lane).
- Free-driving cars pass slow cars and go around held / broken-down ones on
  multi-lane roads; now and then an ambient car stops at the kerb (rightmost
  lane) for 12-40 s. Parked cars are not gridlock-breaker victims.
- CityRide: no taxi spawn within 7 m of another car; the taxi doesn't treat its
  own waiting rider as an obstacle on its last 25 m.
- goal index now follows the path-history trim.

8 sim-minutes x 3 seeds, 60 cars: collisions 0, red runs 0, wrong-lane turns 0,
~300 lane changes, 50-70 overtakes; jam despawns and mean speed unchanged; sim
step cost +3%. All 14 CityRide stands reached (median ~50 s, max 108 s; Hotel del
264 s -> 93 s). test_cityride / test_taxi / test_hitchhike / test_scripted /
test_positions / test_release / test_car_mesh pass.
